       </span>\n                </span> <span class=\"command1\" helpref=\"help-4\">-l</span>\n                    </div>",
      "help": [
        {
          "id": "help-1",
          "text": "print lines that match patterns\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "help-2",
          "text": "-e PATTERNS**, --regexp=**PATTERNS\nUse\nPATTERNS as the patterns. If this option is used multiple times or is combined with the\n-f\n(--file) option, search for all patterns given. This option can be used to protect a pattern beginning with \u201c-\u201d.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "help-0",
          "text": "A pipeline is a sequence of one or more commands separated by one of the control operators\n| or |&. The format for a pipeline is:\n\n[time [-p]] [ ! ] command1 [ [|||&] command2 ... ]\n\nThe standard output of\ncommand1 is connected via a pipe to the stan"
        },
        {
          "id": "help-3",
          "text": "Print newline, word, and byte counts for each FILE, and a total line if more than one FILE is specified\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "help-4",
          "text": "-l, --lines\nprint the newline counts\n"
        }
      ],
